From: Surface Overdrive <noreply@surface-overdrive>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu3: front camera in dim light - steady auto exposure, motion test by brightness, chroma denoise

Auto exposure holds the exposure and analogue gain for changes under 8% and makes them up with the digital
gain: the analogue gain alternated between two 1/16 steps and the picture pulsed by 4% every few frames.
The software temporal denoiser compensates whole-picture brightness changes, remembers the noise from still
moments, measures it per level of brightness, judges blocks with their neighbours, and in dim light a
luma-guided chroma denoise takes away the coloured blotches.
---
